      "hints": [
        "Differentiate: $\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{4x+1}} - 2$.",
        "Integrate: $\\int y\\,dx = \\frac{1}{2}(4x+1)^{3/2} - x^2 + c$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate $y = 3(4x + 1)^{1/2} - 2x$ using the chain rule:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx} = 3\\left( \\frac{1}{2}(4x + 1)^{-1/2} \\times 4 \\right) - 2 = 6(4x + 1)^{-1/2} - 2 = \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{4x + 1}} - 2$$",
        "Integrate $y$ with respect to $x$ using the reverse chain rule:\n$$\\int y\\,dx = 3\\left( \\frac{(4x + 1)^{3/2}}{\\frac{3}{2} \\times 4} \\right) - \\frac{2x^2}{2} + c = \\frac{1}{2}(4x + 1)^{3/2} - x^2 + c$$",
        "State the two calculus expressions:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{4x + 1}} - 2, \\quad \\int y\\,dx = \\frac{1}{2}(4x + 1)^{3/2} - x^2 + c$$"
      ],
